/-!
# Deformations of a formal hypersurface over the dual numbers (Stacks 0DY5(2))

Let `k` be a field, `f` a formal power series in `S = k[[x_1, …, x_n]]` and
`P = S/(f)` the formal hypersurface it cuts out. Tag 0DY5(2) says that the tangent space
`T𝓓_P` of the deformation category of `P` is finite-dimensional over `k` as soon as the
Jacobian ideal `(f, ∂f/∂x_1, …, ∂f/∂x_n)` has radical the ideal generated by the variables.

The source proves it by writing a flat deformation `Q` of `P` over `k[ε]` as
`k[ε][[x_1, …, x_n]]/(f + εg)`: the presentation of `P` by power series lifts to `Q`, which
produces `g`, and changing the lifts `q_i` of the variables changes `g` by
`∑ h_i · ∂f/∂x_i`, so that the deformation is determined by the class of `g` in
`S/(f, ∂f/∂x_1, …, ∂f/∂x_n)`.

This file formalizes the two steps of that argument which concern the presentation:

* the presentation by power series lifts to every square-zero extension of `P` by a finite
  module — the choice of the lifts `q_i`;
* differentiating a principal relation makes the derivative of the relation annihilate every
  conormal functional modulo the functionals that factor through the cotangent complex — the
  change of `g` by `∑ h_i · ∂f/∂x_i`.

Together with
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.Hypersurface.finiteDimensional_of_jacobian_annihilates`, which is the
commutative-algebra half, these are the ingredients of 0DY5(2).

## Main results

* `Stacks.Deformation.isNoetherianRing_compatibleExtension`: a square-zero extension of a
  Noetherian algebra by a finite module is a Noetherian ring.
* `Stacks.Deformation.exists_powerSeries_lift_compatibleExtension`: a map from a formal power
  series algebra into the base of such an extension, carrying the variables into an ideal for
  which the base is adically complete, lifts to the extension.
* `Deformation.Examples.exists_powerSeries_lift_hypersurfaceExtension`: **Stacks 0DY5(2)**, the
  choice of lifts: the power series presentation of a formal hypersurface lifts to every
  square-zero extension of it by a finite module.
* `Algebra.Extension.exists_comp_cotangentComplex_eq_derivation_smul`: **Stacks 0DY5(2)**, the
  derivative relation: for an extension with principal kernel `(f)` and a derivation `D` of its
  presenting ring, `D f` times any conormal functional factors through the cotangent complex.

## Implementation notes

Completeness of the extension is obtained from completeness of its base: the kernel is
nilpotent, so the extension is complete for the kernel, and a Noetherian ring complete for a
nilpotent ideal and for the preimage of a complete ideal downstairs is complete for that
preimage. Noetherianness of the extension is what makes that argument available, and it holds
because the kernel is a finite module over the Noetherian base.

The lifting statement is proved for an arbitrary square-zero extension problem of Tag 08S4
rather than only for the algebra extension problem of Tag 0GPT, which is what lets the fields
`A'`, `B`, `N` of the problem carry their own instances instead of being compared with `k`,
`P`, `N` through the definition of `Stacks.Deformation.algebraExtensionProblem`.

The remaining step of 0DY5(2) — identifying the tangent space, or equivalently
`Ext¹_P(NL_{P/k}, P)`, with the conormal functionals of the power series presentation modulo
the ones factoring through the cotangent complex — is the `ext_cokernel` clause of Tag 0GPU,
`NaiveCotangent.extOne_naiveCotangentComplex_addEquiv_cokernel` of
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.NaiveCotangent.ExtCokernel`, proved there for an arbitrary
`Algebra.Generators`. Part (2) of 0DY5 is therefore stated and proved, as
`Deformation.Examples.hypersurface_finiteDimensional_tangentSpace` of
`StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.RingsHypersurfaceTangentSpaceFinite`.

Tag 0GPU's *extension class* clause is a different clause of that tag, and it is not formalized
here; 0DY5(2) does not use it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY5)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u w

namespace Algebra.Extension

/-- **Stacks 0DY5(2)**, the derivative of the relation. Let `P → B` be an extension whose
kernel is generated by a single element `f`, and let `D` be a derivation of the presenting ring
over the base. Then for every `B`-linear functional `δ` on the conormal module, the multiple
`D f · δ` factors through the cotangent complex of the extension.

In the situation of Tag 0DY5(2) the presenting ring is `k[[x_1, …, x_n]]`, the derivations `D`
are the formal derivatives `∂f/∂x_i`, and the functionals that factor through the cotangent
complex are the ones that do not change the isomorphism class of the deformation. So this is
the statement that changing the lifts of the variables changes the equation of the deformation
by a combination of the `∂f/∂x_i`. -/
theorem exists_comp_cotangentComplex_eq_derivation_smul
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (P : Algebra.Extension A B) (f : P.Ring) (hker : P.ker = Ideal.span {f})
    (D : Derivation A P.Ring P.Ring) (δ : P.Cotangent →ₗ[B] B) :
    ∃ t : P.CotangentSpace →ₗ[B] B,
      (algebraMap P.Ring B (D f)) • δ = t.comp P.cotangentComplex := by
  have hf : f ∈ P.ker := hker ▸ Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_singleton f)
  let c := δ (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk ⟨f, hf⟩)
  let d : Derivation A P.Ring B := (Algebra.linearMap P.Ring B).compDer D
  let t := c • d.liftKaehlerDifferential.liftBaseChange B
  refine ⟨t, ?_⟩
  ext x
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk_surjective x
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mp
    (show x.1 ∈ Ideal.span {f} by rw [← hker]; exact x.property)
  have hx : x = a • (⟨f, hf⟩ : P.ker) := by
    apply Subtype.ext
    simpa [smul_eq_mul, mul_comm] using ha
  have hdf : algebraMap P.Ring B f = 0 := hf
  simp only [LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply,
    Algebra.Extension.cotangentComplex_mk, t, LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul,
    Derivation.liftKaehlerDifferential_comp_D, one_smul]
  rw [hx, map_smul, LinearMap.map_smul_of_tower]
  simp only [d, LinearMap.compDer, Algebra.smul_def, Submodule.coe_smul]
  change algebraMap P.Ring B (D f) * (algebraMap P.Ring B a * c) =
    c * algebraMap P.Ring B (D (a * f))
  simp only [Derivation.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, map_add, map_mul, hdf, zero_mul, add_zero]
  ring

end Algebra.Extension

namespace Stacks.Deformation

/-! ### Noetherianness and completeness of a square-zero extension -/

/-- A surjective ring map with Noetherian target whose kernel is a Noetherian module over the
source has Noetherian source. -/
private theorem isNoetherianRing_of_noetherian_ker
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    (q : A →+* B) (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    [IsNoetherian A (RingHom.ker q)] : IsNoetherianRing A := by
  let : Algebra A B := q.toAlgebra
  let : RingHomSurjective q := ⟨hq⟩
  let e : B →ₛₗ[q] B :=
    { toFun := id
      map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl
      map_smul' := fun _ _ => rfl }
  have : IsNoetherian A B :=
    (e.isNoetherian_iff_of_bijective Function.bijective_id).mpr inferInstance
  exact isNoetherian_of_range_eq_ker (RingHom.ker q).subtype
    (Algebra.linearMap A B) (by rw [Submodule.range_subtype]; rfl)

/-- A solution of a square-zero extension problem whose target is Noetherian and whose module
is finite over that target is a Noetherian ring: its kernel is identified with the module, so it
is Noetherian over the target, hence over the extension itself. -/
theorem isNoetherianRing_compatibleExtension {S : SquareZeroExtensionProblem}
    [IsNoetherianRing S.B] [Module.Finite S.B S.N] (E : S.CompatibleExtension) :
    IsNoetherianRing E.B' := by
  let : RingHomSurjective E.toB.toRingHom := ⟨E.surjective⟩
  have : IsNoetherian S.B (RingHom.ker E.toB.toRingHom) :=
    isNoetherian_of_linearEquiv E.kernelEquiv
  let e : RingHom.ker E.toB.toRingHom →ₛₗ[E.toB.toRingHom] RingHom.ker E.toB.toRingHom :=
    { toFun := id
      map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl
      map_smul' := fun a x => (E.toB_smul_kernel a x).symm }
  have : IsNoetherian E.B' (RingHom.ker E.toB.toRingHom) :=
    (e.isNoetherian_iff_of_bijective Function.bijective_id).mpr inferInstance
  exact isNoetherianRing_of_noetherian_ker E.toB.toRingHom E.surjective

/-- A module is complete for an adic ideal a power of which vanishes. -/
private theorem isAdicComplete_of_pow_eq_bot
    {A M : Type*} [CommRing A] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
    (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ) (hr : I ^ r = ⊥) : IsAdicComplete I M where
  haus' x hx := by simpa [hr] using hx r
  prec' a ha := by
    refine ⟨a r, fun n => ?_⟩
    rcases le_total n r with h | h
    · exact ha h
    · have he : a r = a n := by simpa [hr] using ha h
      rw [he]

/-- Completeness lifts through a nilpotent kernel over a Noetherian ring. -/
private theorem isAdicComplete_of_nilpotent_ker
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (q : A →+* B) (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hker : IsNilpotent (RingHom.ker q)) (J : Ideal A)
    (hB : IsAdicComplete (J.map q) B) : IsAdicComplete J A := by
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hker
  have : IsAdicComplete (RingHom.ker q) A :=
    isAdicComplete_of_pow_eq_bot (RingHom.ker q) r hr
  let e := RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hq
  have he : (J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker q))).map e = J.map q := by
    change Ideal.map e.toRingHom _ = _
    rw [Ideal.map_map]
    rfl
  have hquot : IsAdicComplete (J.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker q)))
      (A ⧸ RingHom.ker q) :=
    (IsAdicComplete.congr_ringEquiv _ e).mp (he.symm ▸ hB)
  apply IsAdicComplete.of_quotient (RingHom.ker q) J
  exact (IsAdicComplete.map_algebraMap_iff J (A ⧸ RingHom.ker q)).mp hquot

/-! ### Lifting a power series presentation through a square-zero extension -/

/-- Maps from finitely many formal variables into a separated adic ring are determined by their
coefficients and by their values on the variables. -/
private theorem powerSeries_ringHom_ext
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] {n : ℕ}
    (J : Ideal B) [IsHausdorff J B]
    (g h : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) A →+* B)
    (hC : ∀ a, g (MvPowerSeries.C a) = h (MvPowerSeries.C a))
    (hX : ∀ i, g (MvPowerSeries.X i) = h (MvPowerSeries.X i))
    (hJ : ∀ i, g (MvPowerSeries.X i) ∈ J) : g = h := by
  have hmod : ∀ r (s : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) A), g s - h s ∈ J ^ r := by
    intro r
    induction r with
    | zero => simp
    | succ r ih =>
      intro s
      have hc : MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff
          (s - MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff s)) = 0 := by simp
      obtain ⟨t, _, ht⟩ :=
        Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.exists_sum_X_mul_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero _ hc
      have hs : s = MvPowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff s) +
          ∑ i, MvPowerSeries.X i * t i := by
        rw [← ht]; ring
      rw [hs, map_add, map_add, hC]
      simp only [add_sub_add_left_eq_sub, map_sum, map_mul, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
      apply Ideal.sum_mem
      intro i _
      rw [← hX, ← mul_sub, pow_succ']
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul (hJ i) (ih (t i))
  ext s
  apply sub_eq_zero.mp
  apply IsHausdorff.haus' (I := J)
  intro r
  simpa using (SModEq.zero.mpr (hmod r s))

/-- Formal variables in an adically complete algebra can be evaluated there. -/
private theorem exists_powerSeries_algHom
    {k B : Type*} [CommRing k] [CommRing B] [Algebra k B]
    {n : ℕ} (J : Ideal B) [IsAdicComplete J B]
    (y : Fin n → B) (hy : ∀ i, y i ∈ J) :
    ∃ g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k →ₐ[k] B,
      ∀ i, g (MvPowerSeries.X i) = y i := by
  let _ : WithIdeal k := ⟨⊥⟩
  have : DiscreteTopology k := is_bot_adic_iff.1 rfl
  let _ : WithIdeal B := ⟨J⟩
  obtain ⟨hcomplete, hhaus⟩ := (IsAdic.isAdicComplete_iff (I := J) rfl).1
    ‹IsAdicComplete J B›
  have := hcomplete
  have := hhaus
  have heval : MvPowerSeries.HasEval y :=
    { hpow := fun i => WithIdeal.isTopologicallyNilpotent_of_mem (hy i)
      tendsto_zero := by simp [Filter.cofinite_eq_bot] }
  let g := MvPowerSeries.eval₂Hom (φ := algebraMap k B)
    continuous_of_discreteTopology heval
  have hg : ⇑g = MvPowerSeries.eval₂ (algebraMap k B) y :=
    MvPowerSeries.coe_eval₂Hom _ _
  refine ⟨{ toRingHom := g, commutes' := ?_ }, ?_⟩
  · intro a
    change g (MvPowerSeries.C a) = algebraMap k B a
    rw [hg]
    exact MvPowerSeries.eval₂_C _ _ _
  · intro i
    change g (MvPowerSeries.X i) = y i
    rw [hg]
    exact MvPowerSeries.eval₂_X _ _ _

/-- A map from a formal power series algebra to a complete quotient lifts across a nilpotent
extension whose source is Noetherian. -/
private theorem exists_powerSeries_lift_of_nilpotent_ker
    {k A B : Type*} [CommRing k] [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra k A] [Algebra k B] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (q : A →ₐ[k] B) (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hker : IsNilpotent (RingHom.ker q.toRingHom))
    (J : Ideal B) [IsAdicComplete J B] {n : ℕ}
    (π : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k →ₐ[k] B)
    (hπ : ∀ i, π (MvPowerSeries.X i) ∈ J) :
    ∃ g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k →ₐ[k] A, q.comp g = π := by
  classical
  let K := J.comap q.toRingHom
  have hK : K.map q.toRingHom = J := Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ hq J
  have : IsAdicComplete K A := isAdicComplete_of_nilpotent_ker q.toRingHom hq hker K
    (hK.symm ▸ ‹IsAdicComplete J B›)
  choose y hy using fun i => hq (π (MvPowerSeries.X i))
  have hyK : ∀ i, y i ∈ K := fun i => by
    change q (y i) ∈ J
    rw [hy i]
    exact hπ i
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_powerSeries_algHom (k := k) K y hyK
  refine ⟨g, ?_⟩
  have he : (q.comp g).toRingHom = π.toRingHom := by
    apply powerSeries_ringHom_ext J
    · intro a
      exact (q.comp g).commutes a |>.trans (π.commutes a).symm
    · intro i
      change q (g (MvPowerSeries.X i)) = π (MvPowerSeries.X i)
      rw [hg, hy]
    · intro i
      change q (g (MvPowerSeries.X i)) ∈ J
      rw [hg, hy]
      exact hπ i
  exact AlgHom.ext fun s => congrArg (fun h : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k →+* B => h s) he

/-- Every solution of a square-zero extension problem with Noetherian target and finite module
admits lifts of maps from a formal power series algebra which carry the variables into an ideal
for which the target is adically complete. -/
theorem exists_powerSeries_lift_compatibleExtension {S : SquareZeroExtensionProblem}
    [IsNoetherianRing S.B] [Module.Finite S.B S.N] (E : S.CompatibleExtension)
    (J : Ideal S.B) [IsAdicComplete J S.B] {n : ℕ}
    (π : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) S.A' →ₐ[S.A'] S.B)
    (hπ : ∀ i, π (MvPowerSeries.X i) ∈ J) :
    ∃ g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) S.A' →ₐ[S.A'] E.B', ∀ s, E.toB (g s) = π s := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing E.B' := isNoetherianRing_compatibleExtension E
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_powerSeries_lift_of_nilpotent_ker
    E.toB E.surjective ⟨2, E.sq_zero⟩ J π hπ
  exact ⟨g, fun s =>
    congrArg (fun h : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) S.A' →ₐ[S.A'] S.B => h s) hg⟩

end Stacks.Deformation

namespace Deformation.Examples

/-- **Stacks 0DY5(2)**, the choice of lifts of the variables. Let `k` be a field, `f` a formal
power series in `k[[x_1, …, x_n]]` and `P = k[[x_1, …, x_n]]/(f)` the formal hypersurface it
cuts out. Then the power series presentation of `P` lifts to every square-zero extension of `P`
by a finite `P`-module.

In the source this is the sentence "we may choose lifts `q_i` of the `x_i`": a flat deformation
`Q` of `P` over the dual numbers is a square-zero extension of `P` by `P`, and the lift
produced here is what presents `Q` as `k[ε][[x_1, …, x_n]]/(f + εg)`. -/
theorem exists_powerSeries_lift_hypersurfaceExtension
    {k : Type w} [Field k] (n : ℕ) (f : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)
    {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N]
    [Module.Finite (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N]
    (E : (Stacks.Deformation.algebraExtensionProblem k
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N).CompatibleExtension) :
    letI : Algebra k E.B' := E.algebraA'B'
    ∃ g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k →ₐ[k] E.B', ∀ s,
      E.toB (g s) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {f}) s := by
  let : Algebra k E.B' := E.algebraA'B'
  let : IsNoetherianRing (Stacks.Deformation.algebraExtensionProblem k
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N).B :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}))
  let : Module.Finite
      (Stacks.Deformation.algebraExtensionProblem k
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N).B
      (Stacks.Deformation.algebraExtensionProblem k
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N).N :=
    inferInstanceAs (Module.Finite (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) N)
  have : IsNoetherianRing E.B' :=
    Stacks.Deformation.isNoetherianRing_compatibleExtension E
  have hm : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)) :=
    MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X k n
  have : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) := by rw [hm]; infer_instance
  have : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) :=
    isAdicComplete_of_iInf_smul_eq_bot _
      (IsHausdorff.iInf_pow_smul (inferInstance : IsHausdorff
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f})))
  have : IsAdicComplete
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)).map
        (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f})))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) :=
    (IsAdicComplete.map_algebraMap_iff _ _).mpr inferInstance
  let q : E.B' →ₐ[k] MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f} :=
    { toRingHom := E.toB.toRingHom
      commutes' := E.toB.commutes }
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := Stacks.Deformation.exists_powerSeries_lift_of_nilpotent_ker
    q E.surjective ⟨2, E.sq_zero⟩
    ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)).map
      (algebraMap (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f})))
    (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k (Ideal.span {f}))
    (fun i => Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (hm ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩))
  exact ⟨g, fun s => congrArg
    (fun h : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k →ₐ[k]
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) => h s) hg⟩

end Deformation.Examples

end
